WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.530
Security analysts often begin investigations inside a SIEM platform.

2
00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:14.128
They review alerts, search logs, build timelines, identify affected users or systems, and determine whether activity is benign or malicious.

3
00:00:14.128 --> 00:00:19.118
A SIEM helps analysts move from a single alert to a broader picture of what happened.

4
00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:25.743
SIEM platforms support threat hunting, incident response, compliance reporting, and operational monitoring.

5
00:00:25.743 --> 00:00:36.199
Analysts may pivot from one event to related information, such as user logins, endpoint activity, network connections, cloud changes, or application logs.

6
00:00:36.199 --> 00:00:43.752
SIEM is not the entire SOC, but it is frequently one of the central tools analysts use during daily operations.

7
00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:52.034
It works best when analysts understand the environment, know what good and bad activity can look like, and keep detections aligned with current risks.
